WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:13.820
the door!"

2
00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:19.383
The next morning Oliver woke up because someone was loudly kicking the front door of the undertaker's shop.

3
00:00:20.243 --> 00:00:21.003
"Open the door!"

4
00:00:21.343 --> 00:00:22.164
cried the voice again.

5
00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:25.985
"Yes, sir," replied Oliver, struggling into his clothes.

6
00:00:26.005 --> 00:00:27.866
"Are you the new boy?"

7
00:00:28.226 --> 00:00:29.487
asked the voice through the keyhole.

8
00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:32.148
"Yes, sir," replied Oliver.

9
00:00:32.984 --> 00:00:35.445
"Then I'll beat you up when I get in, workhouse brat!"

10
00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:39.067
Having made this dreadful promise, the voice began to whistle.

11
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:42.828
Oliver turned the key with a trembling hand and opened the door.

12
00:00:43.689 --> 00:00:45.069
He glanced up and down the street.

13
00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:49.851
But all he could see was an older boy, sitting on a hitching post and eating a slice

14
00:00:49.871 --> 00:00:50.251
of bread.

15
00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:53.513
"I beg your pardon, sir," Oliver said at last.

16
00:00:54.473 --> 00:00:55.153
"Did you knock?"

17
00:00:55.173 --> 00:00:57.334
"I kicked."

18
00:00:58.215 --> 00:00:59.455
"Did you want a coffin, sir?"

19
00:00:59.835 --> 00:01:01.116
Oliver innocently inquired.

20
00:01:02.044 --> 00:01:04.206
"You'll be wanting a coffin soon if you keep this up.

21
00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.688
You don't know who I am, do you?"

22
00:01:07.629 --> 00:01:09.150
The boy jumped down from the post.

23
00:01:10.151 --> 00:01:10.671
"No, sir."

24
00:01:10.691 --> 00:01:14.154
"I'm Mister Noah Claypole, and you work for me.

25
00:01:15.055 --> 00:01:17.176
Take down the shutters, you idle young ruffian."

26
00:01:18.057 --> 00:01:22.641
Noah watched as Oliver struggled to remove the heavy shutters from the windows and stow them beside the

27
00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.583
house, where they were kept during the day.

28
00:01:25.463 --> 00:01:28.886
When Oliver finished, he followed Noah down to the kitchen for breakfast.

29
00:01:28.906 --> 00:01:32.040
"Come sit near the fire, Noah," said Charlotte.

30
00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.402
"I saved you a nice piece of bacon from Master's breakfast."

31
00:01:37.043 --> 00:01:40.924
Then she told Oliver to take some stale bread and sit in the coldest corner of the kitchen.

32
00:01:40.944 --> 00:01:43.986
"Hurry up because Master will want you to mind the shop."

33
00:01:44.006 --> 00:01:46.067
"Do you hear, Workhouse?"

34
00:01:46.507 --> 00:01:47.007
said Noah.

35
00:01:47.888 --> 00:01:48.368
"Hurry up."

36
00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:51.429
"Oh, leave him alone," said Charlotte.

37
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.310
But Noah didn't want to leave Oliver alone.

38
00:01:55.211 --> 00:01:57.352
He finally had someone who ranked below him.

39
00:01:58.292 --> 00:02:01.954
However, the undertaker soon realized that Oliver was someone special.

40
00:02:01.974 --> 00:02:05.396
"Young Twist is a good-looking boy," said Mr.

41
00:02:05.456 --> 00:02:07.317
Sowerberry to his wife one night at supper.

42
00:02:07.337 --> 00:02:10.179
"He should be," replied Mrs.

43
00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:12.540
Sowerberry. "He eats enough."

44
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.543
"There's an expression of melancholy in his face, which is very interesting, my dear.

45
00:02:18.443 --> 00:02:20.544
He'd make a delightful mourner at funerals."

46
00:02:22.185 --> 00:02:24.006
Mrs. Sowerberry looked at him quizzically.

47
00:02:24.026 --> 00:02:28.349
"I don't mean a regular mourner at adult funerals," continued Mr.

48
00:02:28.389 --> 00:02:31.831
Sowerberry. "I'd use him only at children's funerals.

49
00:02:32.971 --> 00:02:36.413
It would be delightful to see a small mourner walking with a small coffin."

50
00:02:37.554 --> 00:02:41.136
Oliver soon had a chance to acquire a great deal of experience as a mourner.

51
00:02:42.076 --> 00:02:45.859
Thanks to an outbreak of measles, he led many processions to the graveyard.

52
00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:49.721
After a month he was formally apprenticed to the undertaker.

53
00:02:50.821 --> 00:02:54.984
Noah was jealous of Oliver's promotion to mourner and so continued to harass him.

54
00:02:56.164 --> 00:02:59.426
One day while they were eating, Noah was determined to make Oliver cry.

55
00:03:00.386 --> 00:03:03.148
The older boy pulled Oliver's hair and pinched his ears.

56
00:03:03.168 --> 00:03:05.689
"Workhouse, how's your mother?"

57
00:03:06.049 --> 00:03:06.550
said Noah.

58
00:03:08.251 --> 00:03:09.892
"She's dead," replied Oliver.

59
00:03:09.912 --> 00:03:12.293
"Don't you say anything about her!"

60
00:03:12.313 --> 00:03:14.794
"What did she die of, Workhouse?"

61
00:03:15.975 --> 00:03:16.875
"Of a broken heart.

62
00:03:17.796 --> 00:03:18.796
That's what I was told."

63
00:03:19.857 --> 00:03:21.378
A tear rolled down Oliver's cheek.

64
00:03:21.398 --> 00:03:23.779
"Oh, what's made you cry?"

65
00:03:23.799 --> 00:03:26.825
"Not you," Oliver replied sharply.

66
00:03:26.845 --> 00:03:29.446
"Don't say anything more about her."

67
00:03:30.446 --> 00:03:33.427
"You might as well know, Workhouse, that your mother was a bad one.

68
00:03:34.308 --> 00:03:36.929
If she hadn't died, she'd have ended up in jail."

69
00:03:37.889 --> 00:03:40.670
Crimson with fury, the little boy overturned the table.

70
00:03:41.671 --> 00:03:43.751
Oliver grabbed Noah and knocked him to the ground.

71
00:03:44.832 --> 00:03:48.093
A minute earlier Oliver had looked like a quiet, dejected creature.

72
00:03:48.914 --> 00:03:51.495
But the insult to his mother had set his blood on fire.

73
00:03:52.455 --> 00:03:53.695
"He's trying to murder me!"

74
00:03:54.096 --> 00:03:54.716
shouted Noah.

75
00:03:56.392 --> 00:03:57.293
"Charlotte! Mrs.

76
00:03:57.353 --> 00:03:58.534
Sowerberry! Help me!

77
00:03:59.575 --> 00:04:00.616
Oliver's gone mad!"

78
00:04:01.657 --> 00:04:03.839
The two women rushed downstairs into the kitchen.

79
00:04:03.859 --> 00:04:05.680
"You little wretch!"

80
00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.202
screamed Charlotte, grabbing Oliver by one arm.

81
00:04:08.222 --> 00:04:11.525
"Oh, you ungrateful, murderous, horrid villain!"

82
00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:14.588
And with every word, she smacked Oliver.

83
00:04:15.629 --> 00:04:17.891
Mrs. Sowerberry and Noah joined in the melee.

84
00:04:18.751 --> 00:04:23.115
The three of them managed to drag the struggling boy into the cellar, where they slammed the door

85
00:04:23.195 --> 00:04:23.976
and locked it tight.

86
00:04:24.976 --> 00:04:27.678
Oliver kicked and kicked the door from the inside.

87
00:04:28.679 --> 00:04:31.662
Mrs. Sowerberry sank into a chair and burst into tears.

88
00:04:31.682 --> 00:04:33.723
"Oh, Charlotte!

89
00:04:34.604 --> 00:04:37.006
It's a blessing we haven't all been murdered in our beds!"

90
00:04:38.047 --> 00:04:39.508
"He'll kick that door down, and Mr.

91
00:04:39.568 --> 00:04:41.590
Sowerberry is away," said Charlotte.

92
00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.892
"Noah, run to Mr.

93
00:04:43.932 --> 00:04:46.614
Bumble and tell him to come here right now," said Mrs.

94
00:04:46.654 --> 00:04:52.859
Sowerberry. Noah ran to the workhouse gate, where he stopped for a moment to make himself look as

95
00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:53.980
pitiful as possible.

96
00:04:54.956 --> 00:04:56.537
Then he shouted, "Mr.

97
00:04:56.617 --> 00:04:57.718
Bumble! Mr.

98
00:04:57.798 --> 00:05:03.762
Bumble!" The parish officer was so alarmed by these cries that he rushed outside with his hat in

99
00:05:03.822 --> 00:05:04.303
his hand.

100
00:05:04.323 --> 00:05:06.244
"What's happened?"

101
00:05:06.544 --> 00:05:07.805
Mr. Bumble said breathlessly.

102
00:05:07.825 --> 00:05:09.766
"Has Oliver run away?"

103
00:05:09.786 --> 00:05:12.889
"No, sir, but he tried to murder us!

104
00:05:13.969 --> 00:05:15.911
Mr. Sowerberry is out, so Mrs.

105
00:05:15.951 --> 00:05:17.932
Sowerberry wants you to come and flog Oliver."

106
00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:21.915
Mr. Bumble put on his hat and tapped his cane on the ground.

107
00:05:21.935 --> 00:05:23.176
"Let's go."

108
00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:28.740
They hurried to the undertaker's shop, where Oliver was still kicking the cellar door and Mrs.

109
00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.922
Sowerberry and Charlotte were waiting in fear.

110
00:05:30.942 --> 00:05:33.324
"Oliver!" shouted Mr.

111
00:05:33.344 --> 00:05:34.345
Bumble through the keyhole.

112
00:05:36.066 --> 00:05:36.927
"Let me out!"

113
00:05:37.888 --> 00:05:39.409
"Do you know who's speaking to you?"

114
00:05:39.429 --> 00:05:42.892
"Yes." "Aren't you afraid of me?"

115
00:05:42.912 --> 00:05:46.014
"No!" Oliver replied boldly.

116
00:05:47.035 --> 00:05:49.017
Mr. Bumble staggered back in surprise.

117
00:05:49.037 --> 00:05:51.879
"He must be mad," said Mrs.

118
00:05:53.488 --> 00:05:55.989
Sowerberry. "No boy in his right mind would dare speak to you like that."

119
00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.351
"It's not madness, ma'am.

120
00:05:59.371 --> 00:05:59.932
It's meat.

121
00:06:00.832 --> 00:06:03.534
If you had kept the boy on gruel, this never would have happened."

122
00:06:04.594 --> 00:06:05.435
Just then Mr.

123
00:06:05.455 --> 00:06:06.495
Sowerberry returned.

124
00:06:07.536 --> 00:06:11.498
After hearing what Oliver had done, he dragged the boy from the cellar and beat him.

125
00:06:12.578 --> 00:06:13.719
Mr. Bumble shook his head.

126
00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:17.721
"All you can do now is leave him in the cellar for a day or so until he's

127
00:06:17.741 --> 00:06:18.582
a little starved.

128
00:06:19.482 --> 00:06:22.544
Then take him out and keep him on gruel through his apprenticeship."

129
00:06:24.168 --> 00:06:27.571
So they left Oliver in the cellar for the rest of the day with a slice of bread

130
00:06:27.651 --> 00:06:28.271
and some water.

131
00:06:29.352 --> 00:06:30.093
That night Mrs.

132
00:06:30.133 --> 00:06:31.994
Sowerberry ordered him upstairs to bed.

133
00:06:33.195 --> 00:06:37.698
As he looked around the dismal undertaker's workshop, Oliver fell on his knees and wept.

134
00:06:38.799 --> 00:06:43.022
For a long time, he remained motionless, but finally he got up and opened the door.

135
00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:48.326
Outside, it was a cold, dark night, and the stars seemed very far away.

136
00:06:49.507 --> 00:06:50.868
Oliver softly closed the door.

137
00:06:51.948 --> 00:06:54.630
He tied up his few articles of clothing into a handkerchief.

138
00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.531
Then he sat on a bench to wait for morning.

139
00:06:58.512 --> 00:07:02.274
When the first ray of daylight struggled through the shutters, Oliver opened the door.

140
00:07:03.274 --> 00:07:04.995
He took one last look around the shop.

141
00:07:06.016 --> 00:07:07.697
Then he stepped out into the street.
